      "topic": "chem",
      "summary": "Magnesium coordination polymers with flexible aliphatic linkers enter an ordered mesophase as solvent is removed. Linker mobility then allows glass formation without melting. Measurements distinguish this pathway from melt-quenching, which partially disrupts coordination and gives a less stiff glass.",
      "whyRelevant": "Shows how linker dynamics can control solid-state processing while retaining connectivity.",
