      "summary": "Postsynthetic annulation converts imine linkages into cationic imidazopyridinium units in a cobalt porphyrin framework. The change stabilizes the lattice and positions bromide near cobalt sites. The authors use the resulting framework for light-driven conversion of carbon dioxide and epoxides to cyclic carbonates.",
